"""Action results slide."""

from surface import Attribute, Frame, NodeKind, Slide, Surface, TeachingStep, cell, code, code_block, group, heading, line_break, paragraph, prose, row, span, strong, table, text

pub def action_results() -> Slide:
    return Slide(
        slug="action-results",
        title="What does an action ask for?",
        frame=Frame.ActionDetail,
        subtitle="Same four sales: books 25 · games 40 · books 15 · music 10",
        content=[
            group([
                group([
                    code_block("""from pyspark.sql import functions as F

books = sales.filter(
    F.col("category") == "books")""", style="ar-definition"),
                    code_block("books.show(5)", style="ar-call ar-show"),
                    code_block("number_of_books = books.count()", style="ar-call ar-count"),
                    code_block("books.write.parquet(\"output/books\")", style="ar-call ar-write"),
                ], style="ar-code"),
                group([
                    group([
                        heading("A DataFrame"),
                        prose("books", style="ar-variable"),
                        paragraph([
                            text("Keep rows where"),
                            line_break(),
                            code("category == \"books\""),
                        ], style="ar-condition"),
                        prose("The filtered rows have not been computed.", style="ar-detail"),
                    ], style="ar-result ar-defined"),
                    group([
                        heading("Displayed rows"),
                        table([
                            Surface(kind=NodeKind.Caption, content="The two books sales displayed by show", style="sr-only"),
                            Surface(kind=NodeKind.TableHead, children=[
                                row([
                                    cell([
                                        text("category"),
                                    ], header=true),
                                    cell([
                                        text("amount"),
                                    ], header=true),
                                ]),
                            ]),
                            Surface(kind=NodeKind.TableBody, children=[
                                row([
                                    cell([
                                        text("books"),
                                    ]),
                                    cell([
                                        text("25"),
                                    ]),
                                ]),
                                row([
                                    cell([
                                        text("books"),
                                    ]),
                                    cell([
                                        text("15"),
                                    ]),
                                ]),
                            ]),
                        ], style="ar-preview"),
                        prose("Up to 5 rows. Order shown is illustrative.", style="ar-detail"),
                        paragraph([
                            text("Python return: "),
                            code("None"),
                        ], style="ar-return"),
                    ], style="ar-result ar-displayed"),
                    group([
                        heading("A value in Python"),
                        prose("number_of_books", style="ar-variable-name"),
                        prose("2", style="ar-number"),
                        prose("An integer: the number of books sales.", style="ar-detail"),
                    ], style="ar-result ar-counted"),
                    group([
                        heading("Files in storage"),
                        paragraph([
                            code("output/books/"),
                        ], style="ar-directory"),
                        group([
                            strong("Parquet data files"),
                            span("The two books rows are saved here."),
                        ], style="ar-file-result"),
                        prose("The output can contain multiple files.", style="ar-detail"),
                        paragraph([
                            text("Python return: "),
                            code("None"),
                        ], style="ar-return"),
                    ], style="ar-result ar-written"),
                    group([
                        heading("Return values and effects"),
                        table([
                            Surface(kind=NodeKind.TableBody, children=[
                                row([
                                    cell([
                                        text("show(5)"),
                                    ], header=true),
                                    cell([
                                        text("Returns "),
                                        code("None"),
                                        text("."),
                                        line_break(),
                                        text("Displays the two books rows."),
                                    ]),
                                ]),
                                row([
                                    cell([
                                        text("count()"),
                                    ], header=true),
                                    cell([
                                        text("Returns the integer "),
                                        strong("2"),
                                        text("."),
                                    ]),
                                ]),
                                row([
                                    cell([
                                        text("write"),
                                    ], header=true),
                                    cell([
                                        text("Returns "),
                                        code("None"),
                                        text("."),
                                        line_break(),
                                        text("Writes Parquet files."),
                                    ]),
                                ]),
                            ]),
                        ]),
                    ], style="ar-summary"),
                ], style="ar-output", attributes=[Attribute(name="aria-live", value="polite")]),
            ], style="ar-layout"),
        ],
        lesson_style="action-requests",
        steps=[
            TeachingStep(label="Define books",
                heading="What have we created?",
                explanation="A new DataFrame describing the books sales. Assigning it to a variable has not materialised the rows."),
            TeachingStep(label="Display rows",
                heading="show() asks for a preview.",
                explanation="Spark executes the work needed to display up to five rows."),
            TeachingStep(label="Count rows",
                heading="count() asks for a number.",
                explanation="Spark counts the matching rows. Python receives the integer 2."),
            TeachingStep(label="Write files",
                heading="A batch write is also an action.",
                explanation="Spark executes the work needed to save the result in storage."),
        ],
        notes="""Continue from the classification exercise. Reuse the same four-row sales DataFrame from Spark is Lazy: books25, games40, books15 and music10. It is an existing DataFrame backed by our Parquet example, with category and amount columns, and has not been cached. F is explicitly imported. Do not switch to a new createDataFrame syntax or introduce the later five-row sales example yet.

Define books: ask what the variable contains. The transformation returns a new DataFrame representing a query, without materialising its result rows. The sales DataFrame is unchanged. Query analysis or source metadata work can already occur; this is not a claim that the driver has done absolutely nothing.

Display: reveal show(5). Spark displays up to five matching rows. There are two in this illustrative input. The table order is not guaranteed; no orderBy is present. show returns None, not a Python list of those rows, and it need not compute every partition for a limited preview. It can issue more than one job.

Count: reveal the assignment and the Python integer 2. This is DataFrame.count(), the action, not GroupedData.count(). The output is a number of rows, not the amount total 40.

Write: reveal the batch write. The output path denotes a Parquet dataset location and can contain multiple part files. We are not illustrating a single file per row or an exact number of tasks/files. On successful completion, write.parquet returns None to Python; creating files is its side effect. The full result is written to storage rather than collected into the Python variable. The default write mode errors if the destination already exists; use a fresh output path for an actual demonstration. This deck does not execute the write. All actions remain subject to their own optimised plan.

Transition: We have requested three results from the same books DataFrame. Does that mean Spark computed it once and kept it?
https://spark.apache.org/docs/4.2.0/api/python/reference/pyspark.sql/api/pyspark.sql.DataFrame.filter.html
https://spark.apache.org/docs/4.2.0/api/python/reference/pyspark.sql/api/pyspark.sql.DataFrame.show.html
https://spark.apache.org/docs/4.2.0/api/python/reference/pyspark.sql/api/pyspark.sql.DataFrame.count.html
https://spark.apache.org/docs/4.2.0/api/python/reference/pyspark.sql/api/pyspark.sql.DataFrameWriter.parquet.html""",
    )
